# FUTURE — nice-to-have follow-ups (`./mf`)

- `thread view` does not fetch background report bodies, change trails or live
  child activity; its `inputs` block says `"not fetched"` for them
  (`src/commands/thread/`). Fetch them through the shared chat session once it
  owns those surfaces, so the CLI draws what the app draws.

- `liveView` deliberately reports `not_observed / rewritten` when the join read seeds text.
  Per-block provenance could distinguish read-owned prefixes from stream-owned suffixes if
  that diagnostic limitation becomes costly. Do not add a shadow transcript; the shared sync
  would own the refinement (L1 design §5 in the mf-client-unification work item).

- `Session.request` returns `unknown` unless the caller passes a `parse` option. Only the snapshot read is validated,
  through the contracts' snapshot validator. The ~30 other callers in `tools/mf/src/commands/` cast the `unknown`
  explicitly (`as SendMessageResponse`, `as AdmissionLookup`, ...). None of those casts can produce a false success,
  because send and tail prove from the validated snapshot, but a malformed response fails with a `TypeError`
  instead of a classified read error. Pass `parse` with a contracts schema as each route gains one; don't add a
  CLI-only schema.
